## Concept Overview

Blue-green deployment maintains two identical production environments, enabling zero-downtime deployments by routing traffic between them while Terraform manages infrastructure state and consistency.

## Implementation Details

- **Workspaces**: Create dedicated `blue` and `green` Terraform workspaces with identical infrastructure configurations
- **State Management**: Configure remote backend with state locking to prevent concurrent modifications and ensure state consistency
- **Atlantis Integration**: Set up PR-based workflows that deploy to the inactive workspace first, with automated validation and approval gates
- **Traffic Routing**: Implement load balancer target groups to seamlessly switch traffic after passing comprehensive health checks

## Code Example

```hcl
# workspace configuration
terraform {
  backend "remote" {
    organization = "your-org"
    workspaces {
      blue = "blue-prod"
      green = "green-prod"
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This assesses practical multi-cloud Terraform coordination, provider aliasing, per-cloud backends, and gating across tenants.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-cloud provider configuration with aliasing
- Per-cloud backends and remote state isolation
- CI gates that validate plans across clouds
- Enforcing region constraints and mandatory tagging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton Terraform-like snippet demonstrating provider aliases and cloud map
variable "cloud" { type = string; description = "aws or gcp" }

provider "aws" {
  region = lookup(var.cloud_map, var.cloud, {})["aws_region"]
}
provider "google" {
  region = lookup(var.cloud_map, var.cloud, {})["gcp_region"]
}

module "tenant_network" {
  source = "./modules/network"
  cloud  = var.cloud
}
```

